  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between isorhamnetin 3-O-2''-glucosylrhamnoside and SQ20B, mediated through hepatocytes. This relationship is supported by multiple pathways, where the compound acts as a target for several entities, including (R)-b-(Boc-amino)-2,5-difluorobenzenebutanoic acid and Cocosamide B, both of which have a target relationship with SQ20B. Additionally, the compound is linked to Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, which in turn targets Nudiposide, which also targets SQ20B. These findings collectively indicate that isorhamnetin 3-O-2''-glucosylrhamnoside may serve as a functional intermediary in the signaling or regulatory pathways leading to SQ20B activity. The evidence is consistent across different pathways, suggesting a plausible mechanism of action, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
